  "worked_solution": "First, note that\n\n$$\n\u00ac(\u00acQ\u21d2\u00acP)\u2261\u00ac(\u00ac(\u00acQ)\u2228\u00acP).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n\u00ac(\u00ac(\u00acQ)\u2228\u00acP)\u2261\u00ac(Q\u2228\u00acP).\n$$\n\nWe can distribute the negation over the disjunction using De Morgan's law:\n\n$$\n\u00ac(Q\u2228\u00acP)\u2261\u00acQ\u2227\u00ac(\u00acP).\n$$\n\nCanceling out double negations, we reach\n\n$$\n\u00acQ\u2227\u00ac(\u00acP)\u2261\u00acQ\u2227P.\n$$\n\nSo the given statement is equivalent to $P\u2227\u00acQ.$",
